{"availability":"available","full":"winebarrel/pistachio","name":"pistachio","description":"pistachio is a declarative schema management tool for PostgreSQL with a Terraform-like plan/apply workflow.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":58,"forks":1,"created":"2026-02-21T01:22:56Z","updated":"2026-10-04T07:33:42Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://winebarrel.github.io/pistachio/","topics":["cli","database-migration","database-migrations","db-migration","ddl","declarative","declarative-migrations","golang","postgres","postgresql","schema-management","schema-migration","schema-migrations"],"demo":"https://pistachio-demo.winebarrel.workers.dev/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:58.621Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:58.621Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:58.621Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:58.621Z","stars":58,"forks":1}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["pistachio is a declarative schema management tool for PostgreSQL with a Terraform-like plan/apply workflow, built on pgquerygo. Define the desired schema in SQL, and pistachio generates the DDL diff.","pistachio manages a PostgreSQL schema from SQL files. The files contain the whole schema as DDL, in the form that pista dump writes. pista plan reads the database catalog and compares it with the files. It then prints the DDL that makes the database match the files. pista apply runs that DDL. pista dump writes the files from a database that you already have.","The playground runs pista diff on two schemas that you edit in the page. There is nothing to install."],"features":["An object removed from the file is dropped only when --allow-drop includes its type. Until then, the plan shows the drop as a -- skipped: comment. See Controlling drops.","-- pista:renamed-from oldname above an object changes a drop and a create into a RENAME. See Renaming objects.","apply --with-tx runs the plan in one transaction. -- pista:concurrently marks an index for CONCURRENTLY, which cannot run in a transaction. --try-tx handles both cases. See Transactions and locks.","plan --explain reports which statements scan or rewrite a table, what they block, and how big the table is. See Explaining a plan.","plan --out writes a plan file. apply-from runs it later, and refuses to run if the database changed in between. See Plan files."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winebarrel/pistachio/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"2ac4b9db2ff506f5ac4042528aebad904291635f8934c556d4de01a55ec64391","extractedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:33.668Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:33.668Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"pistachio is a declarative schema management tool for PostgreSQL with a Terraform-like plan/apply workflow, built on pgquerygo. Define the desired schema in SQL, and pistachio generates the DDL diff.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winebarrel/pistachio/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"2ac4b9db2ff506f5ac4042528aebad904291635f8934c556d4de01a55ec64391","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winebarrel/pistachio/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:33.668Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-04T07:33:42Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/winebarrel/pistachio/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T08:11:33.669Z","hash":"2ac4b9db2ff506f5ac4042528aebad904291635f8934c556d4de01a55ec64391","originalBytes":5805,"storedBytes":5805,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["pista","plan","schema","see","pistachio","run","schema.sql","apply","database","ddl","file","files","files.","runs","sql","table","bash","column","create","dump","object","postgresql","add","drop","email","every","index","management","objects","prints","there","winebarrel","writes","allow-drop","alter","becomes","changed","changes","commands","composite","concurrently","database.","diff","docker","domains","dropped","ed